From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: the machine's hive file is closed to people too (9101)

On Windows the SOFTWARE and SYSTEM hive files are SYSTEM's and
Administrators'; people read HKLM through the registry, key by key as each
key's descriptor allows. The shared prefix's system.reg was 0644 in the
Wine group: any person could read every HKLM value whatever its key
allowed them. It is now one of the hives 9100 keeps 0600 (written so,
closed when loaded). The server is its only reader besides root's tools
(sg-firewall's daemon, sg-location); sg-session closes it at boot too.

Gate test/hiveprivate-gate.sh. Mutant: SG_MUTANT_SYSTEM_HIVE_SHARED.
---
--- a/server/registry.c
+++ b/server/registry.c
@@ -2404,6 +2404,13 @@
     return 0;
 #endif
     if (!strcmp( filename, "user.reg" )) return 1;
+    /* 9101: the machine's hive too. On Windows the SOFTWARE and SYSTEM hive
+     * files are SYSTEM's and Administrators' (users read HKLM through the
+     * registry, which checks each key's descriptor); readable here, a person
+     * could read every HKLM value whatever its key allowed them. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SYSTEM_HIVE_SHARED
+    if (!strcmp( filename, "system.reg" )) return 1;
+#endif
     return len > 9 && !strncmp( filename, "user-", 5 ) && !strcmp( filename + len - 4, ".reg" );
 }
 
